About the role
We are looking for a hands-on Principal Software Development Engineer to help shape the future of our Store Operations technology platforms. This role combines strategic technical leadership with practical software engineering. You will work across a complex landscape of services, APIs, infrastructure and engineering teams, helping to simplify the platform, reduce operational complexity and improve engineering effectiveness. This is not an architecture governance role and it is not a role that operates independently of delivery teams. Success depends on working collaboratively with engineers, architects, product teams and stakeholders to develop solutions that teams understand, support and ultimately own. You will provide technical leadership, challenge thinking, facilitate decision-making and help teams align around a shared technical direction. You will remain hands-on, contributing code, solving complex technical problems, building prototypes and helping teams deliver high-quality software at scale. 

You will be responsible for
Key Responsibilities• Define and evolve the technical strategy for Store Operations platforms in partnership with engineering teams. • Lead the simplification and modernisation of a complex technology estate, reducing technical debt, operational burden and unnecessary complexity. • Work collaboratively with teams to design scalable, resilient and maintainable solutions that can be confidently built, operated and supported. • Remain actively involved in software engineering through coding, design reviews, prototyping and technical problem solving. • Improve engineering effectiveness through better tooling, automation, developer experience, platform capabilities and engineering practices. • Champion modern software engineering practices, including AI-assisted development, intelligent automation and agentic tooling, helping teams improve productivity, quality and delivery outcomes. • Improve platform reliability, observability, operational excellence and long-term maintainability. • Coach, mentor and influence engineers across multiple teams, raising technical standards and strengthening engineering capability

You will need
What We're Looking For• Significant experience designing, building and evolving large-scale distributed systems and platforms. • Strong software engineering background with the ability to contribute high-quality production code. • Proven experience simplifying complex technology estates and driving architectural evolution. • Experience influencing technical direction across multiple teams and organisations without direct authority. • Strong understanding of architecture, platform engineering, DevOps, reliability and operational excellence. • Excellent communication, collaboration and stakeholder management skills. • A pragmatic approach to technology decisions, balancing innovation with reliability, maintainability and business outcomes. • Passion for engineering excellence, continuous improvement and modern software engineering practices. ________________________________________Success in This RoleYou will be successful when: • The Store Operations platform is simpler, more scalable and easier to maintain. • Engineering teams are more productive and able to deliver value faster. • Operational complexity and support overhead have been significantly reduced. • Reliability, resilience and observability have improved. • Teams have adopted effective modern engineering practices, including appropriate use of intelligent automation and AI-assisted development. • Technical decisions are made collaboratively and are actively supported by the teams that own and operate the technology. 
Role SummaryA hands-on Principal Engineer who works with engineering teams to simplify a complex Store Operations platform, improve engineering effectiveness, and introduce modern software engineering practices through technical leadership, collaboration and software delivery. 

Whats in it for you?

