Job summary&nbsp; 

We are seeking a Power Platform Developer to join our Managed Services team and work with our clients to deliver high-quality business applications and automation solutions. &nbsp; 

The ideal candidate will have 4-6 years of relevant experience in Microsoft Power Platform development, with a strong focus on Power Apps, Power Automate, integrations, application support, and continuous improvement. The candidate should be passionate about solving business problems through scalable, secure, and efficient low-code solutions. 

&nbsp; 

General: Responsibilities and tasks for this role &nbsp; 

- Develop and maintain Microsoft Power Apps applications, including Canvas and Model-Driven Apps. &nbsp; 
 - Design, develop, and maintain automated workflows using Power Automate cloud flows and desktop flows. &nbsp; 
 - Integrate Power Platform solutions with SharePoint, Microsoft 365, Microsoft Teams, Dataverse, SQL Server, and other enterprise systems. &nbsp; 
 - Design and implement third-party integrations using REST APIs, custom connectors, and web services. &nbsp; 
 - Develop reusable components and custom web resources to extend Power Apps functionality where required. &nbsp; 
 - Ensure timely ticket follow-up and resolution of L2 incidents within defined SLAs. &nbsp; 
 - Perform root cause analysis (RCA) for production incidents and implement corrective and preventive measures. &nbsp; 
 - Monitor application and workflow performance, proactively identify issues, and implement improvements. &nbsp; 
 - Handle change requests, enhancements, and bug fixes for existing Power Platform solutions. &nbsp; 
 - Collaborate with L1 support, development teams, and business stakeholders to resolve complex technical issues and translate business requirements into effective technical solutions. &nbsp; 
 - Coordinate operational support and maintenance activities for client accounts. &nbsp; 
 - Test and optimise Power Platform solutions for performance, scalability, reliability, and reusability. &nbsp; 
 - Follow Power Platform security, governance, compliance, and development best practices. &nbsp; 
 - Maintain technical documentation, including solution designs, configuration details, deployment guides, and support procedures. &nbsp; 
 - Provide clear and timely communication to end-users and stakeholders regarding incident resolutions, changes, and maintenance schedules. &nbsp; 
 - Support client onboarding and service transition activities by providing technical expertise, guidance, and knowledge transfer. &nbsp; 
 - Participate in the complete software development lifecycle (SDLC) and identify opportunities for process improvement and automation. &nbsp; 
 - Knowledge Sharing & Team Development: Train team members, share technical expertise, and guide Power Apps, Power Automate, and development best practices to support team growth and continuous improvement. &nbsp; &nbsp; 

Must-have qualifications & competencies&nbsp; 

- Minimum of 4-6 years of experience in Microsoft Power Platform development, particularly Power Apps and Power Automate. &nbsp; 
 - Strong experience developing Canvas Apps and Model-Driven Apps, including forms, galleries, reusable components, responsive layouts, and customisations. &nbsp; 
 - Proficiency in Power Fx, including advanced formulas, collections, variables, Patch, SubmitForm, data validation, and error handling. &nbsp; 
 - Experience with Power Automate cloud flows and desktop flows, including approvals, scheduled flows, automated triggers, expressions, loops, and exception handling. &nbsp; 
 - Good understanding of Microsoft Dataverse, including table design, relationships, data modelling, business rules, and security roles. &nbsp; 
 - Experience integrating Power Apps and Power Automate with SharePoint, Microsoft 365, SQL Server, and other enterprise systems. &nbsp; 
 - Strong knowledge of REST/SOAP APIs, HTTP actions, JSON, custom connectors, and third-party system integrations. &nbsp; 
 - Understanding of delegation, application performance optimisation, debugging, and troubleshooting using Power Apps Monitor and Power Automate run history. &nbsp; 
 - Experience with Power Platform solutions, managed and unmanaged solutions, environment variables, connection references, security, and deployment across development, UAT, and production environments. &nbsp; 
 - Good understanding of Power Platform architecture, governance, licensing, and DLP policies, along with experience in production support, root cause analysis (RCA), and continuous improvement. &nbsp; &nbsp; 

Nice to have qualifications & competencies&nbsp; 

- Experience with UiPath, Automation Anywhere&nbsp; 
 - Knowledge of Python, PowerShell, VBScript, or similar scripting languages&nbsp; 
 - Experience with AI/IDP tools (e. g. , Document Automation, AI Builder)&nbsp; 
 - Exposure to CI/CD, DevOps, or ITIL-based service management practices&nbsp; &nbsp; 

Certification&nbsp; 

- PL-500 Microsoft Power Automate RPA Developer (Advanced/Master)&nbsp; 
 - Any RPA-related certification&nbsp; &nbsp; 

What we offer&nbsp; 

- Tailored development plan with career coaching&nbsp; 
 - Regular feedback - we value your opinion, and we appreciate new ideas&nbsp; 
 - International career and project opportunities&nbsp; 
 - Deepen your working knowledge of intelligent automation through our structured training courses&nbsp; &nbsp; 
